course: dictionary
lesson: 9922
title: Tangle: a knot or a mess
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A tangle is a twisted, messy knot of hair, string, wires or other long things. «When they bow, their curly wigs get tangled, and Alice has to run off to hide her laughter.» Tangled here means the wigs have become twisted together in a knot.
explain: Tangle can also be a verb: to tangle is to twist things together so they are hard to pull apart. Ask yourself: does the sentence talk about things getting knotted, or about a muddle? That tells you which meaning fits.
explain: Tangle can also mean a confused or difficult situation. Informally, to tangle with someone means to get into a fight or argument with them. Read the words around the word to find out which meaning is right.
fact: A tangle is a twisted, messy knot of hair, string, wires or other long things.
fact: To tangle is to twist things together so they are hard to pull apart.
fact: «Tangled» means knotted or twisted together, as in «tangled roots».
fact: A tangle can also be a confused or difficult situation.
fact: «Fishing line can tangle animals» means it can knot around them and trap them, so always pick up litter.
exercise: «Her headphone wire was in a tangle.» What does tangle mean here? | A small, sharp bite | A long walk | A quiet sound | *A twisted, messy knot
exercise: «The mangrove's tangled roots break the waves and hold the soil.» What does tangled suggest about the roots? | *Twisted together in a messy knot | Shiny and smooth | Empty and hollow | Very short
exercise: Ali says «to tangle» means to pull things neatly apart. Is Ali right? | No, to tangle means to sing loudly | Yes, to tangle means to pull things neatly apart | Yes, it means to swim fast | *No, to tangle means to twist things so they are hard to pull apart
test: «Fishing line can tangle animals and hurt them.» What does tangle mean in this sentence? | To swim beside them fast | To sing to them loudly | To pull them apart neatly | *To twist around them so they are hard to free
test: Which informal phrase means to get into a fight or argument with someone? | in a tangle | tangled up | *tangle with someone | tangling wires
exam: «Bats do not get tangled in people's hair.» What does tangled mean in this sentence? | Clean and shiny | Very wet from rain | *Caught up in knotted hair, twisted together | Flying very fast
